  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Norway-CAFOD Strategic Partnership 2018-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Norway and CAFOD have identified that it is mutually beneficial to enter into a strategic partnership, the basis of which is outlined in the Memorandum of Understanding. Mutual benefits will be realised as the two agencies work together across a number of organisational functions with a view to enhancing and developing each organisation&#x2019;s ability to deliver its humanitarian function. While the primary function of the MoU remains around joint humanitarian working, we will work to ensure we share cross organisation information and on our advocacy and development programmes and, where appropriate, develop joint working. A range of specific activities will be agreed mutually and be delivered in partnership, with a particular focus on:

- Institutional humanitarian fund-raising and joint humanitarian programming, 
- Humanitarian advocacy, 
- Humanitarian Capacity Building,
- Joint surge capacity development,
- Peace and reconciliation programming, 
- Joint country focus. 

The anticipated outcomes arising from this partnership will include greater humanitarian and, where appropriate development programme impact, organisational strengthening, enhanced organisational effectiveness and operational efficiencies.</narrative>
  </description>
